# Android SDK location (required). Android Studio sets this automatically.
sdk.dir=/path/to/android-sdk

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# There is no service URL to configure.
#
# This file used to document EARSLATE_WORKER_URL, pointing at a session broker
# on api.classeve.com. That broker was removed in 0.4.0 and its route now 404s:
# earslate mints session credentials on-device from the user's own provider key
# and has no backend of any kind. A debug build needs nothing here but sdk.dir.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Release signing.
#
# All four properties must be set to produce a Play-uploadable release APK.
# There is NO fallback: the `verifyReleaseSigning` task fails the build when any
# of them is missing or when the keystore file does not exist. (This file
# previously claimed the build falls back to the debug keystore. It does not,
# and has not since that task was added — a debug-signed artifact that looks
# like a release is exactly what fail-closed exists to prevent.)
#
# The keystore must be the shared brand keystore, whose DN is
# `CN=<App>, O=ClassEve, C=IN` and nothing else. `verifyReleaseIdentity` runs
# after every assembleRelease and fails the build on any other DN, or on entity
# strings anywhere in the APK's raw bytes.
#
# Generate the keystore once with:
#
#   keytool -genkeypair -v \
#     -keystore /absolute/path/to/earslate-release.keystore \
#     -alias earslate \
#     -keyalg RSA -keysize 2048 -validity 10000
#
# Use a strong password — back it up to a password manager. Losing this
# keystore means losing the ability to ship updates of this app on Play.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# EARSLATE_STORE_FILE=/absolute/path/to/earslate-release.keystore
# EARSLATE_STORE_PASSWORD=...
# EARSLATE_KEY_ALIAS=earslate
# EARSLATE_KEY_PASSWORD=...
